Let's write the implementation. I'll use the flat list of rolls approach.

Key validation requirements:
- Negative roll: "Negative roll is invalid"
- Pin count exceeds the pins on the lane: "Pin count exceeds pins on the lane"
- Rolling after game over: "Cannot roll after game is over"
- Scoring before game over: "Score cannot be taken until the end of the game"

Per-frame validation logic:
- Frames 1–9: first roll is 0–10. Second roll must not exceed 10 - first.
- Frame 10: first roll is 0–10. If first roll is 10 (strike), two bonus rolls are allowed. Second bonus roll: if the first bonus roll is not a strike, the second must not exceed 10 - first bonus. If the first bonus is a strike, the second can be anything 0–10.
- Game ends when: frames 1–9 are complete (each frame is 1 or 2 rolls), and the rolls in frame 10 are complete.

Implementation: keep a list of rolls. Track frame count and rolls within the current frame.

Let's write it:

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class BowlingGame {
    private static final int PINS = 10;
    private static final int FRAMES = 10;

    private final List<Integer> rolls = new ArrayList<>();
    private int frame = 1;
    private int rollsInFrame = 0;
    private int pinsDownInFrame = 0;
    private boolean gameComplete = false;

    public void roll(int pins) {
        if (gameComplete) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Cannot roll after game is over");
        }
        if (pins < 0) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Negative roll is invalid");
        }
        if (pins > PINS) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Pin count exceeds pins on the lane");
        }

        if (frame < FRAMES) {
            // frames 1-9
            if (rollsInFrame == 1 && pinsDownInFrame + pins > PINS) {
                throw new IllegalStateException("Pin count exceeds pins on the lane");
            }
            rolls.add(pins);
            rollsInFrame++;
            pinsDownInFrame += pins;
            if (pinsDownInFrame == PINS || rollsInFrame == 2) {
                frame++;
                rollsInFrame = 0;
                pinsDownInFrame = 0;
            }
        } else {
            // frame 10
            if (rollsInFrame == 0) {
                rolls.add(pins);
                rollsInFrame = 1;
                pinsDownInFrame = pins;
                if (pins < PINS) {
                    rollsInFrame = 2; // need a second roll to finish the frame
                    // actually set pending
                }
            } else if (rollsInFrame == 1) {
                if (pinsDownInFrame < PINS && pinsDownInFrame + pins > PINS) {
                    throw new IllegalStateException("Pin count exceeds pins on the lane");
                }
                rolls.add(pins);
                rollsInFrame = 2;
                pinsDownInFrame += pins;
                if (pinsDownInFrame < PINS) {
                    gameComplete = true;
                }
            } else {
                // third roll (only reachable if first was a strike)
                rolls.add(pins);
                rollsInFrame = 3;
                gameComplete = true;
            }
        }
    }

    public int score() {
        if (!gameComplete) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Score cannot be taken until the end of the game");
        }
        int total = 0;
        int i = 0;
        for (int f = 1; f <= FRAMES; f++) {
            if (rolls.get(i) == PINS) {
                total += PINS + rolls.get(i + 1) + rolls.get(i + 2);
                i += 1;
            } else if (rolls.get(i) + rolls.get(i + 1) == PINS) {
                total += PINS + rolls.get(i + 2);
                i += 2;
            } else {
                total += rolls.get(i) + rolls.get(i + 1);
                i += 2;
            }
        }
        return total;
    }
}
```

